[{:db/id "q-15405/selection/f28838f531f3de85c0079a1c4dcd989da7dd68d2ad4cc2ef87f3959758ae3804" :answer/id #uuid "f000f73e-e82a-5621-94da-35fee0550957" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{1+4{cos}^{4}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-15405/selection/f2c661a51d21e4c56fcd21017c9c049c90548a596e3b7993ff9533a60a90b0db" :answer/id #uuid "69369c60-36e9-5995-b2f4-0974a1b7acd3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{1+4{sin}^{2}⁡(2x)}\\,\\text{d}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-15405/selection/5336deff64ef152d004622f9bcc18b11e46c9d4709136e06aa919dda12950006" :answer/id #uuid "f2395032-bbe5-5dc7-baec-910b13602072" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{1+16{cos}^{4}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-15405/selection/9fbddaebf27ff4f673a10e1e7c5ab8aa1ac66c966668d3253592738ff2137147" :answer/id #uuid "b21b4783-aa49-5d41-ae9d-2e144b9f8a43" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{1+16{sin}^{2}⁡(2x)}\\,\\text{d}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-15405/selection/ac54fce78f664685100013a6578e140648bc9449260ac0573adb381a2bc83c97" :answer/id #uuid "4aab0848-19ea-5f74-8bca-790848eaecd1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{1+16{sin}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-15405/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "f904054a-52e2-5724-a79c-646dff7d72f5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-15405/selection/9fbddaebf27ff4f673a10e1e7c5ab8aa1ac66c966668d3253592738ff2137147" :answer-field/choices ["q-15405/selection/f28838f531f3de85c0079a1c4dcd989da7dd68d2ad4cc2ef87f3959758ae3804" "q-15405/selection/f2c661a51d21e4c56fcd21017c9c049c90548a596e3b7993ff9533a60a90b0db" "q-15405/selection/5336deff64ef152d004622f9bcc18b11e46c9d4709136e06aa919dda12950006" "q-15405/selection/9fbddaebf27ff4f673a10e1e7c5ab8aa1ac66c966668d3253592738ff2137147" "q-15405/selection/ac54fce78f664685100013a6578e140648bc9449260ac0573adb381a2bc83c97"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-15405" :question/id #uuid "898e2d00-d1c0-5287-b1c1-c8753234b0c5" :question/math-academy-id "q-15405" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14082094/assets/f74f28bf0b5bf2208b3cebf837c667cf9a9ae737d7eb758708a98548ffca8e3a.png)\n\nWhich of the following gives the length of the curve $y=4{sin}^{2}⁡x$ on $[-\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\frac{\\pi }{2}],$ as shown above?" :question/worked-solution "The arc length of a curve $y=f(x)$ between $x=a$ and $x=b$ can be found using the formula\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{a}^{b}\\sqrt{1+[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $f(x)=4{sin}^{2}⁡x,$ $a=-\\frac{\\pi }{2},$ and $b=\\frac{\\pi }{2}.$\n\nFirst, we find the derivative of $f(x):$\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=4\\cdot 2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${f}^{′}(x)=4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)$ into the arc length formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{1+{[{f}^{′}(x)]}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{1+16{sin}^{2}⁡(2x)}\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-15405/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "965026e6-db46-5930-8844-c423e6ea795a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-15405"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-6001/selection/4c35c473016d633433e4a08276f7cf7eb01801542efbe9f442c6599a82a7a15a" :answer/id #uuid "fa08814c-ef55-5679-8dac-0f5e4701bb17" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{1}^{e}\\sqrt{2{ln}^{2}⁡x+\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+2}\\,\\text{d}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-6001/selection/c20a895900b2c6d36c09f723f3f3165d54ea3604d3f6295fb6f3e309c17526e0" :answer/id #uuid "eb74e63a-336e-5857-9d13-94aafe1b39a7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{1}^{e}\\sqrt{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+2}\\,\\text{d}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-6001/selection/c2824be891fecf2823a63817e3943e37ceafb354a3d841c32814cff2105bee7d" :answer/id #uuid "208fbe3b-e9d9-5313-a671-3c5e77ed8076" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{1}^{e}\\sqrt{2{ln}^{2}⁡x+\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+1}\\,\\text{d}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-6001/selection/f0f114b96d48f473744f9ca4b32b33b59af8190c9292e35a7f40c66c6267edb7" :answer/id #uuid "08c07a39-c64a-5c5c-8eef-6b63f67e79f6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{1}^{e}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+1\\,\\text{d}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-6001/selection/1018727d554b3ec8c483695461e1c4d28699f4d11bf57137bdbe5a20c482d953" :answer/id #uuid "85c58e77-01db-58f4-a1af-93af085a6d82" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{1}^{e}\\sqrt{{ln}^{2}⁡x+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+2}\\,\\text{d}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-6001/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "2b36a1ad-cc83-5720-9512-b6cd29c942c9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-6001/selection/1018727d554b3ec8c483695461e1c4d28699f4d11bf57137bdbe5a20c482d953" :answer-field/choices ["q-6001/selection/4c35c473016d633433e4a08276f7cf7eb01801542efbe9f442c6599a82a7a15a" "q-6001/selection/c20a895900b2c6d36c09f723f3f3165d54ea3604d3f6295fb6f3e309c17526e0" "q-6001/selection/c2824be891fecf2823a63817e3943e37ceafb354a3d841c32814cff2105bee7d" "q-6001/selection/f0f114b96d48f473744f9ca4b32b33b59af8190c9292e35a7f40c66c6267edb7" "q-6001/selection/1018727d554b3ec8c483695461e1c4d28699f4d11bf57137bdbe5a20c482d953"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-6001" :question/id #uuid "1018367e-83ad-5af3-99ec-2abf57016cee" :question/math-academy-id "q-6001" :question/problem "The length of the curve $y=x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x$ on $[1,e]$ is given by" :question/worked-solution "The arc length of a curve $y=f(x)$ between $x=a$ and $x=b$ can be found using the formula\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{a}^{b}\\sqrt{1+[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $f(x)=x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x,$ $a=1,$ and $b=e.$\n\nFirst, we find the derivative of $f(x):$\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+x\\cdot \\frac{1}{x}=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+1\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${f}^{′}(x)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+1$ into the arc length formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{1}^{e}\\sqrt{1+[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{e}\\sqrt{1+{(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+1)}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{e}\\sqrt{{ln}^{2}⁡x+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+2}\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-6001/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "965026e6-db46-5930-8844-c423e6ea795a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-6001"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-6000/selection/7b9c23769acbfb5c430dcc0fe413527fcacd1835dc2576c4bd719e3ddeff6330" :answer/id #uuid "abe59f73-92ec-5adc-80e4-69b8717d28a3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{1}^{9}\\sqrt{1+9x\\sqrt[3]{x}}\\,\\text{d}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-6000/selection/0300367fb1931a97c7688af75f4fdf7341253141b621318081fdf2246d2adabd" :answer/id #uuid "dfe835db-c824-5736-ba79-0a0057ae6d64" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{1}^{9}\\sqrt{\\frac{3\\sqrt[3]{x}}{x}}\\,\\text{d}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-6000/selection/31bd725b5bd3daf30fda60f5fac26c24f4702b9d064881cbf76e881a987e7a7e" :answer/id #uuid "a7005d7d-f080-5ad1-b6f6-4689db032325" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{1}^{9}\\sqrt{1+\\frac{1}{9x\\sqrt[3]{x}}}\\,\\text{d}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-6000/selection/cb6e45d6948b129cc0885b09a817a50a01446bf7d6c734137945eef2a594bef9" :answer/id #uuid "50734827-1745-569d-b07c-e927ba0a9ee6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{1}^{9}\\sqrt{1+\\frac{1}{3\\sqrt[3]{{x}^{2}}}}\\,\\text{d}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-6000/selection/fc6a7c6277da754ff63fc8dd58c2a49f4706191b93de5d13f090941e778f331d" :answer/id #uuid "698b1bc5-19f7-522d-aef2-d12b0ad1c586" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{1}^{9}\\sqrt{\\frac{9}{\\sqrt[3]{x}}}\\,\\text{d}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-6000/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "829978b1-d0e2-55f5-8907-fef6802eee0a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-6000/selection/31bd725b5bd3daf30fda60f5fac26c24f4702b9d064881cbf76e881a987e7a7e" :answer-field/choices ["q-6000/selection/7b9c23769acbfb5c430dcc0fe413527fcacd1835dc2576c4bd719e3ddeff6330" "q-6000/selection/0300367fb1931a97c7688af75f4fdf7341253141b621318081fdf2246d2adabd" "q-6000/selection/31bd725b5bd3daf30fda60f5fac26c24f4702b9d064881cbf76e881a987e7a7e" "q-6000/selection/cb6e45d6948b129cc0885b09a817a50a01446bf7d6c734137945eef2a594bef9" "q-6000/selection/fc6a7c6277da754ff63fc8dd58c2a49f4706191b93de5d13f090941e778f331d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-6000" :question/id #uuid "75f3ee9a-aa46-5e51-9545-c1a50545e935" :question/math-academy-id "q-6000" :question/problem "The length of the curve $y=\\sqrt[3]{x}$ on $[1,9]$ is given by" :question/worked-solution "The arc length of a curve $y=f(x)$ between $x=1$ and $x=9$ can be found using the formula\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{a}^{b}\\sqrt{1+[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $f(x)=\\sqrt[3]{x},$ $a=1,$ and $b=9.$\n\nFirst, we find the derivative of $f(x):$\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=\\frac{1}{3\\sqrt[3]{{x}^{2}}}\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${f}^{′}(x)=\\frac{1}{3\\sqrt[3]{{x}^{2}}}$ into the arc length formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{1}^{9}\\sqrt{1+[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{9}\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{1}{3\\sqrt[3]{{x}^{2}}})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{9}\\sqrt{1+\\frac{1}{9x\\sqrt[3]{x}}}\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-6000/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "965026e6-db46-5930-8844-c423e6ea795a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-6000"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-51270/selection/25df0294a24e7c70fef8a954fbf10e924abf9fe7d752dc4bfe500ff68aff0f68" :answer/id #uuid "a953e404-68ed-5802-9fcc-bc892f73a8ba" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{-\\pi /4}^{\\pi /3}\\sqrt{{cot}^{4}⁡x+1}\\,\\text{d}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-51270/selection/fbcb2994e9b062cde240383456c9b2c69a0d6c16fb9fb455878a92fd0db59c44" :answer/id #uuid "39e901d5-0d91-5fb0-8e9a-43af7eed520e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{-\\pi /4}^{\\pi /3}\\sqrt{{sin}^{2}⁡x-{cos}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-51270/selection/fee4b02e5017c866023fb9c69abbb7b513dec1d9519c45162d02c7fb720a17c3" :answer/id #uuid "b99215f4-7394-5ffd-91c6-6a67ef6a4ff3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{-\\pi /4}^{\\pi /3}\\sqrt{{sec}^{2}⁡x+1}\\,\\text{d}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-51270/selection/863617f99ae692a717ebb95619ba47e4a941357dbbe3d9c9af1ae747b6b54fd3" :answer/id #uuid "f7f67879-67cf-5397-8314-9e41e7f438c0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{-\\pi /4}^{\\pi /3}\\sqrt{1+{sec}^{4}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-51270/selection/e7b3e2e7318df34fc5d2e53bb670d321616d5a48404f1045837acc084ae395fc" :answer/id #uuid "30ee5108-4913-52ff-9a03-401ef77cfe5c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{-\\pi /4}^{\\pi /3}\\sqrt{{cot}^{2}⁡x+1}\\,\\text{d}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-51270/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "7a7b1185-6d92-5063-a513-69478aae2c6a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-51270/selection/863617f99ae692a717ebb95619ba47e4a941357dbbe3d9c9af1ae747b6b54fd3" :answer-field/choices ["q-51270/selection/25df0294a24e7c70fef8a954fbf10e924abf9fe7d752dc4bfe500ff68aff0f68" "q-51270/selection/fbcb2994e9b062cde240383456c9b2c69a0d6c16fb9fb455878a92fd0db59c44" "q-51270/selection/fee4b02e5017c866023fb9c69abbb7b513dec1d9519c45162d02c7fb720a17c3" "q-51270/selection/863617f99ae692a717ebb95619ba47e4a941357dbbe3d9c9af1ae747b6b54fd3" "q-51270/selection/e7b3e2e7318df34fc5d2e53bb670d321616d5a48404f1045837acc084ae395fc"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-51270" :question/id #uuid "d49288fb-58db-5dbb-bf7b-d975ead2b1e6" :question/math-academy-id "q-51270" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14082094/assets/87dc32f8909ac1c05adc981b4133a3f6e721918e4aca6923b08a073d2fb8cfe9.png)\n\nWhich of the following gives the length of the curve $y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡x$ on $[-\\frac{\\pi }{4},\\frac{\\pi }{3}],$ as shown above?" :question/worked-solution "The arc length of a curve $y=f(x)$ between $x=a$ and $x=b$ can be found using the formula\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{a}^{b}\\sqrt{1+[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $f(x)=\\operatorname{tan}⁡x,$ $a=-\\frac{\\pi }{4},$ and $b=\\frac{\\pi }{3}.$\n\nFirst, we find the derivative of $f(x):$\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)={sec}^{2}⁡x\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${f}^{′}(x)={sec}^{2}⁡x$ into the arc length formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{-\\pi /4}^{\\pi /3}\\sqrt{1+{[{f}^{′}(x)]}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\pi /4}^{\\pi /3}\\sqrt{1+{sec}^{4}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-51270/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "965026e6-db46-5930-8844-c423e6ea795a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-51270"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-353191/field-1/8c9c1dbb0ce6fc22ea16e209f1b3cf9b728dd1195e256f6b2f7bbb6c05317bec" :answer/id #uuid "1a267970-fb52-5c96-bbf8-30c567eef7db" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1+\\ln(3)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-353191/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "2f625505-43f9-5735-96aa-6a3eb36b033f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-353191/field-1/8c9c1dbb0ce6fc22ea16e209f1b3cf9b728dd1195e256f6b2f7bbb6c05317bec" :answer-field/choices ["q-353191/field-1/8c9c1dbb0ce6fc22ea16e209f1b3cf9b728dd1195e256f6b2f7bbb6c05317bec"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-353191" :question/id #uuid "e41c732f-7225-5d09-880d-7d7b833ee64e" :question/math-academy-id "q-353191" :question/problem "Compute the arc length of $y=\\frac{{x}^{2}}{8}-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5x)$ for $x\\in [1,3].$ Do not round the answer.\n\n$L=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The arc length of a curve $y=f(x)$ between $x=a$ and $x=b$ can be found using the formula\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{a}^{b}\\sqrt{1+[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $f(x)=\\frac{{x}^{2}}{8}-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5x),$ $a=1,$ and $b=3.$\n\nFirst, we find the derivative of $f(x):$\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=\\frac{x}{4}-\\frac{1}{x}\n$$\n\nNow, let's compute $\\sqrt{1+[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}}:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{1+[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}} & =\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{x}{4}-\\frac{1}{x})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1+(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{16}-\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}})} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{{x}^{2}}{16}+\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{{x}^{4}+8{x}^{2}+16}{16{x}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{({x}^{2}+4)^{2}}{16{x}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{2}+4}{4x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $\\sqrt{1+[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}}=\\frac{{x}^{2}+4}{4x}$ into the arc length formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}\\sqrt{1+[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}\\frac{{x}^{2}+4}{4x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}(\\frac{x}{4}+\\frac{1}{x})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{8}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)|}_{1}^{3} \\\\  & =[\\frac{{3}^{2}}{8}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡3]-[\\frac{{1}^{2}}{8}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡1] \\\\  & =1+\\operatorname{ln}⁡3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-353191/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f87bc14d-5e68-5a5e-bec8-f1b5b21c02e8"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-353191"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-85665"] :question/problem "Compute the arc length of $y=\\frac{1}{2}({e}^{x}+{e}^{-x})$ for $x\\in [0,\\operatorname{ln}⁡2].$" :question/worked-solution "The arc length of a curve $y=f(x)$ between $x=a$ and $x=b$ can be found using the formula\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{a}^{b}\\sqrt{1+[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $f(x)=\\frac{1}{2}({e}^{x}+{e}^{-x}),$ $a=0,$ and $b=\\operatorname{ln}⁡2.$\n\nFirst, we find the derivative of $f(x):$\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=\\frac{1}{2}({e}^{x}-{e}^{-x})\n$$\n\nNow, let's compute $\\sqrt{1+[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{1+[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}} & =\\sqrt{1+{[\\frac{1}{2}({e}^{x}-{e}^{-x})]}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1+\\frac{1}{4}({e}^{2x}-2+{e}^{-2x})} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{4}({e}^{2x}+2+{e}^{-2x})} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{4}{({e}^{x}+{e}^{-x})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}({e}^{x}+{e}^{-x})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $\\sqrt{1+[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}}=\\frac{1}{2}({e}^{x}+{e}^{-x})$ to the formula for the arc length, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\sqrt{1+[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}({e}^{x}+{e}^{-x})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}({e}^{x}-{e}^{-x}){|}_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[({e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}-{e}^{-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2})-({e}^{0}-{e}^{-0})] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[2-\\frac{1}{2}-0] \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-352924/field-1/e0ede232c229e1df030a73a1aa70c95f2619852a039e06705f5c9276faed0349" :answer/id #uuid "1916daff-8ec2-549c-89d4-471a53de781f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{e^{2}-e^{-2}}{8}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-352924/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "7839e8fd-b1aa-5a55-8b22-9ada1841643a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-352924/field-1/e0ede232c229e1df030a73a1aa70c95f2619852a039e06705f5c9276faed0349" :answer-field/choices ["q-352924/field-1/e0ede232c229e1df030a73a1aa70c95f2619852a039e06705f5c9276faed0349"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-352924" :question/id #uuid "ff72803f-2d3d-5cc6-b5c3-fcf617357553" :question/math-academy-id "q-352924" :question/problem "Compute the arc length of $y=\\frac{{e}^{4x}+{e}^{-4x}}{8}$ for $x\\in [0,\\frac{1}{2}].$ Do not round the answer.\n\n$L=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The arc length of a curve $y=f(x)$ between $x=a$ and $x=b$ can be found using the formula\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{a}^{b}\\sqrt{1+[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $f(x)=\\frac{{e}^{4x}+{e}^{-4x}}{8},$ $a=0,$ and $b=\\frac{1}{2}.$\n\nFirst, we find the derivative of $f(x):$\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=\\frac{{e}^{4x}-{e}^{-4x}}{2}\n$$\n\nNow, let's compute $\\sqrt{1+[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}}\\,:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{1+[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}} & =\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{{e}^{4x}-{e}^{-4x}}{2})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1+\\frac{{e}^{8x}-2+{e}^{-8x}}{4}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{{e}^{8x}+2+{e}^{-8x}}{4}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{({e}^{4x}+{e}^{-4x})^{2}}{4}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{4x}+{e}^{-4x}}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $\\sqrt{1+[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}}=\\frac{{e}^{4x}+{e}^{-4x}}{2}$ into the arc length formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{0}^{1/2}\\sqrt{1+[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1/2}\\frac{{e}^{4x}+{e}^{-4x}}{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={(\\frac{{e}^{4x}-{e}^{-4x}}{8})|}_{0}^{1/2} \\\\  & =[\\frac{{e}^{4(1/2)}-{e}^{-4(1/2)}}{8}]-[\\frac{{e}^{4(0)}-{e}^{-4(0)}}{8}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}({e}^{2}-\\frac{1}{{e}^{2}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{4}-1}{8{e}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-352924/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f87bc14d-5e68-5a5e-bec8-f1b5b21c02e8"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-352924"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-362543/field-1/5521c093c4d60c23d630a99bc791ac7318f4615e164361df756510ffc0408a97" :answer/id #uuid "39ca2ec5-8a34-50d2-a165-7227d126a5ee" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{14}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-362543/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "25b10528-df5c-5479-b078-dad4157f08bb" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-362543/field-1/5521c093c4d60c23d630a99bc791ac7318f4615e164361df756510ffc0408a97" :answer-field/choices ["q-362543/field-1/5521c093c4d60c23d630a99bc791ac7318f4615e164361df756510ffc0408a97"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-362543" :question/id #uuid "b4767432-922a-5be8-be5b-18e91bf8210c" :question/math-academy-id "q-362543" :question/problem "Compute the arc length $L$ of $y=\\frac{2}{3}(x-3)^{3/2}$ for $x\\in [3,6].$ Do not round the answer.\n\n$L=$ \n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The arc length of a curve $y=f(x)$ between $x=a$ and $x=b$ can be found using the formula\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{a}^{b}\\sqrt{1+[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $f(x)=\\frac{2}{3}(x-3)^{3/2},$ $a=3,$ and $b=6.$\n\nFirst, we find the derivative of $f(x):$\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=\\frac{2}{3}\\cdot \\frac{3}{2}(x-3)^{1/2}=\\sqrt{x-3}\n$$\n\nNow, let's compute $\\sqrt{1+[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}}:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{1+[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}} & =\\sqrt{1+{[\\sqrt{x-3}]}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1+(x-3)} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{x-2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $\\sqrt{1+[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}}=\\sqrt{x-2}$ to the formula for the arc length, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{3}^{6}\\sqrt{1+[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{3}^{6}\\sqrt{x-2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={(\\frac{2}{3}(x-2)^{3/2})|}_{3}^{6} \\\\  & =[\\frac{2}{3}(6-2)^{3/2}]-[\\frac{2}{3}(3-2)^{3/2}] \\\\  & =\\frac{16}{3}-\\frac{2}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{14}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-362543/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f87bc14d-5e68-5a5e-bec8-f1b5b21c02e8"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-362543"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-82616/selection/7628f311f01c4aaa54f2414adfab72b075ab5d150bf407ba8552d99d13a24cbc" :answer/id #uuid "91e0efce-7970-5889-b19f-8b881fa5c09e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=2+\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-82616/selection/cf7622cd76f320566446a078fddcab9c9af58f59078661e0cd642e396e9ab6ed" :answer/id #uuid "726a300f-c2d6-5c5c-90e8-1f673dd48c92" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\sqrt{2}+\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-82616/selection/87ec67b58d886543866898f49f9150642850bcbc518ee533401406d66b2d66de" :answer/id #uuid "3507f5be-3820-52e2-bac3-811e6a93755b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(1-{x}^{2})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-82616/selection/d300c23ff006a8780ce428d5aa9622073c6ebac5deca3df6134f2de9ff3f27b5" :answer/id #uuid "36bdb045-5075-5d8e-9b5b-25d6e4979ebb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\sqrt{2}-\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-82616/selection/a468176ad754f8ba04cc4998467d92ae5b74e0b8d4dbfe648f5c60a055f8827f" :answer/id #uuid "eae7ea55-0ff8-5a7a-b787-d86136150866" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(x+1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-82616/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "6a1fbe26-7b49-5b03-a95c-68dd80ec0e4f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-82616/selection/d300c23ff006a8780ce428d5aa9622073c6ebac5deca3df6134f2de9ff3f27b5" :answer-field/choices ["q-82616/selection/7628f311f01c4aaa54f2414adfab72b075ab5d150bf407ba8552d99d13a24cbc" "q-82616/selection/cf7622cd76f320566446a078fddcab9c9af58f59078661e0cd642e396e9ab6ed" "q-82616/selection/87ec67b58d886543866898f49f9150642850bcbc518ee533401406d66b2d66de" "q-82616/selection/d300c23ff006a8780ce428d5aa9622073c6ebac5deca3df6134f2de9ff3f27b5" "q-82616/selection/a468176ad754f8ba04cc4998467d92ae5b74e0b8d4dbfe648f5c60a055f8827f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-82616" :question/id #uuid "2465b53b-d454-5ce5-bc18-251befc3123f" :question/math-academy-id "q-82616" :question/problem "The length of a curve $y=f(x)$ is given by ${\\int }_{-1/2}^{1/2}\\sqrt{1+\\frac{1}{1-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x.$ Which of the following could be  an equation for this curve?" :question/worked-solution "The arc length of a curve $y=f(x)$ between $x=a$ and $x=b$ can be found using the formula\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{a}^{b}\\sqrt{1+[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe're given that \n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{-1/2}^{1/2}\\sqrt{1+\\frac{1}{1-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nComparing the above with the arc length formula, we see that we must have\n\n$$\n[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}=\\frac{1}{1-{x}^{2}}\\,⟹\\,{f}^{′}(x)=\\pm \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}.\n$$\n\nIntegrating the above equation with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\pm \\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}\\text{ d}x \\\\  & =\\pm \\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the given options, the only one that has the required form is $y=\\sqrt{2}-\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-82616/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "55f783c4-25d6-5855-877e-31bed16b12c4"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-82616"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-82639/selection/626aaab3dab8581e88f6d5156ff3fed354a9d8e3ff2f081250ebc8ec7c0f5470" :answer/id #uuid "f1212beb-4cff-5f08-b365-9c5fdc91561d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=3\\sqrt{x}-6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-82639/selection/24af185c69b5f14488511b4b7e6f6691ec6f5390671ef4bad3fa2a62fd5bc450" :answer/id #uuid "633b907e-f199-5825-9546-8fc2bea6ce64" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-82639/selection/c0a065756a3eac87ef9185a6f351a26d2e8afe0e2f98ac4a4400686f27fc7f61" :answer/id #uuid "e972a5dd-b734-589d-ae62-e56c0c98d599" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}}+2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-82639/selection/631afe65ef1cbf852139b87b727d9a7031bc3851d4dffa6460b0e0fe1519e411" :answer/id #uuid "1c0df7f5-977a-5c32-b067-c2c04160369e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\sqrt{{x}^{3}}-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-82639/selection/39f5ea0e85c777a8083c2285437d15e34019fb8025e565a3bfe3990f27eb1eb6" :answer/id #uuid "81811a9f-6050-541e-9579-ad6e6ef455c7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=-2\\sqrt{{x}^{3}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-82639/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "09ab57cc-af45-5f62-bd67-c166dd3b3717" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-82639/selection/39f5ea0e85c777a8083c2285437d15e34019fb8025e565a3bfe3990f27eb1eb6" :answer-field/choices ["q-82639/selection/626aaab3dab8581e88f6d5156ff3fed354a9d8e3ff2f081250ebc8ec7c0f5470" "q-82639/selection/24af185c69b5f14488511b4b7e6f6691ec6f5390671ef4bad3fa2a62fd5bc450" "q-82639/selection/c0a065756a3eac87ef9185a6f351a26d2e8afe0e2f98ac4a4400686f27fc7f61" "q-82639/selection/631afe65ef1cbf852139b87b727d9a7031bc3851d4dffa6460b0e0fe1519e411" "q-82639/selection/39f5ea0e85c777a8083c2285437d15e34019fb8025e565a3bfe3990f27eb1eb6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-82639" :question/id #uuid "70181cb8-d0db-5bb5-b812-c66d19c2730e" :question/math-academy-id "q-82639" :question/problem "The length of a curve $y=f(x)$ is given by ${\\int }_{0}^{1}\\sqrt{1+9x}\\,\\text{d}x.$ Which of the following could be  an equation for this curve?" :question/worked-solution "The arc length of a curve $y=f(x)$ between $x=a$ and $x=b$ can be found using the formula\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{a}^{b}\\sqrt{1+[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe're given that \n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\sqrt{1+9x}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nComparing the above with the arc length formula, we see that we must have\n\n$$\n[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}=9x\\,⟹\\,{f}^{′}(x)=\\pm 3\\sqrt{x}.\n$$\n\nIntegrating the above equation with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\pm 3\\int \\sqrt{x}\\text{ d}x \\\\  & =\\pm 2\\sqrt{{x}^{3}}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the given options, the only one that has the required form is $y=-2\\sqrt{{x}^{3}}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-82639/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "55f783c4-25d6-5855-877e-31bed16b12c4"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-82639"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-122391/selection/315c08897c5a21096c657c55eca49a0de026c1fe2413610cbc300d7b858ff59c" :answer/id #uuid "406028df-0352-560b-9b42-264aa756c1a6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=-\\sqrt{3-2{x}^{2}}+\\sqrt{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122391/selection/91c086fb4df634fdbfd9ed2ab690da5f274ec62251c68b99b6b3d28c02d00675" :answer/id #uuid "1534a69f-f3d9-5b03-8edb-768a987593bd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=-\\sqrt{1-2{x}^{2}}+\\sqrt{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122391/selection/6ccf3991ba400a3be245d48276cc748d0802c101b1c24f90ac8f31daddd11f7a" :answer/id #uuid "47a372f6-4233-5266-93f3-ef8753a1eb85" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=-\\sqrt{3-2x}+\\sqrt{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122391/selection/adf7041a7499cc0de73df68cafd19dbd9e0b071b6572b56e28bb1d883f772de1" :answer/id #uuid "cd1aa5b0-9c65-56ac-bb38-4174d31bdf2f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=-\\sqrt{2-{x}^{3}}+\\sqrt{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122391/selection/fcdf66776505fe98e8e4a91af142a9d5ef0f300f917bd1202286dbe32e86cc17" :answer/id #uuid "2e775025-e28f-5a75-b066-0119bf43609d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=-\\sqrt{3+{x}^{2}}+\\sqrt{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122391/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "38800ebd-2861-5022-8a8b-fee3be9419b9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-122391/selection/315c08897c5a21096c657c55eca49a0de026c1fe2413610cbc300d7b858ff59c" :answer-field/choices ["q-122391/selection/315c08897c5a21096c657c55eca49a0de026c1fe2413610cbc300d7b858ff59c" "q-122391/selection/91c086fb4df634fdbfd9ed2ab690da5f274ec62251c68b99b6b3d28c02d00675" "q-122391/selection/6ccf3991ba400a3be245d48276cc748d0802c101b1c24f90ac8f31daddd11f7a" "q-122391/selection/adf7041a7499cc0de73df68cafd19dbd9e0b071b6572b56e28bb1d883f772de1" "q-122391/selection/fcdf66776505fe98e8e4a91af142a9d5ef0f300f917bd1202286dbe32e86cc17"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-122391" :question/id #uuid "e9f04453-3f40-58db-b58f-2274524d2d22" :question/math-academy-id "q-122391" :question/problem "The length of a curve $y=f(x)$ is given by ${\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\sqrt{1+\\frac{4{x}^{2}}{3-2{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x.$ Which of the following could be  an equation for this curve?" :question/worked-solution "The arc length of a curve $y=f(x)$ between $x=a$ and $x=b$ can be found using the formula\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{a}^{b}\\sqrt{1+[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe're given that \n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\sqrt{1+\\frac{4{x}^{2}}{3-2{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nComparing the above with the arc length formula, we see that we must have\n\n$$\n[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}=\\frac{4{x}^{2}}{3-2{x}^{2}}\\,⟹\\,{f}^{′}(x)=\\pm \\frac{2x}{\\sqrt{3-2{x}^{2}}}.\n$$\n\nIntegrating the above equation with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\pm \\int \\frac{2x}{\\sqrt{3-2{x}^{2}}}\\text{ d}x \\\\  & =\\pm \\sqrt{3-2{x}^{2}}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the given options, the only one that has the required form is $y=-\\sqrt{3-2{x}^{2}}+\\sqrt{2}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-122391/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "55f783c4-25d6-5855-877e-31bed16b12c4"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-122391"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-560"] :question/problem "Compute the arc length of  the curve $y=x^{3/2}$ between the points $x=0$ and $x=\\dfrac{4}{3},$ as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14082094/assets/4ed8b94a4fff3c22697264e467f955f2e51a62618d03295c4e4f38493bff2ced.png)" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
